course: dictionary
lesson: 9387
title: One word, many meanings: spray
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Spray can be a noun or a verb. As a noun it can mean many tiny drops in the air, or a can that pushes out liquid. As a verb it means to send out liquid in tiny drops. «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster» uses the drops in the air, because sea spray is the salty mist blown up from the waves.
explain: Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning. «Keepers sometimes spray perfume or spices in an enclosure» is about sending out drops, so spray is a verb here. «A nasal spray» is a bottle, so spray is a noun. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or an action?
explain: Context also tells you whether a word is safe or risky. Cleaning sprays, insect sprays and paint sprays can harm you, so never spray them in your eyes or near a flame, and use them only with an adult. «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid» shows that spray can also be a way animals protect themselves. Ask yourself what the sentence is warning you about.
fact: Spray can be a noun (a spray) or a verb (to spray).
fact: «Spray» as a noun can mean many tiny drops of liquid flying through the air, like sea spray from waves.
fact: «A spray» can also mean a can or bottle that pushes out liquid in tiny drops, such as hair spray or bug spray.
fact: A spray of flowers is a small bunch of them, so spray can also describe a neat bunch of flowers.
fact: Phrases with spray include spray paint, sunscreen spray, nasal spray and spray bottle.
exercise: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster.» What does spray mean here? | A small bunch of flowers | A can that pushes out liquid | * Tiny drops of salty water flying through the air | To paint a wall
exercise: «Keepers sometimes spray perfume or spices in an enclosure.» What does spray mean here? | To sing very loudly | * To send out a liquid in tiny drops | A bottle of medicine for the nose | A small bunch of flowers
exercise: «Antihistamine tablets, nasal sprays or eye drops help hay fever.» What is a nasal spray? | A tablet you swallow with water | A cloud of sea salt | A bunch of flowers for your nose | * A bottle that pushes medicine out in tiny drops into your nose
test: Why should you use cleaning sprays only with an adult? | * Some sprays can harm you, especially near your eyes or a flame | Sprays are always sweet-smelling and safe | Sprays are only for flowers | Sprays make you taller
test: Which phrase means a small bunch of flowers? | sea spray | spray paint | nasal spray | * a spray of flowers
exam: In «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid», spray is a verb. What does it mean? | To fly through the air like a bird | A small bunch of flowers | * To send out a liquid in tiny drops | To be quiet and still
